  H4.chest.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    An old chest bound with iron bands. The lid has a latch, but no lock.
  H4.chest.open_done narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The chest is open: an old coverlet and Dunya's odds and ends. The bell clapper is gone now.
  H4.bed.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Dunya's narrow bed, with a patchwork quilt. Made up just as it was when she was here.
  H4.bed.left_M23a narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    see Tamara as she hands out the letters
  H4.bed.left_M23b narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    call on Pavel at the mill
  H4.bed.left_M23c narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    see Mama at Dunya's house
  H4.bed.left_M23d narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    talk to Tikhon about Dunya
  H4.v02.done narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Light beneath the roof. Familiar things still in their familiar places.
  H1.wave.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The place by Dunya's stove. Mama can't see or hear me through the glass. But perhaps she has something that remembers this house?
  M1.schedule.use narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The mill rules have faded. The bell marked the start and end of each shift — and sent signals at the sluice: "One strike — go. Two — stop. A long ring — raise."
  M1.schedule.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The mill rules give bell signals: "One strike — go. Two — stop. A long ring — raise."
  M1.wheel.look_still narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The pond is drained. No water reaches the wheel, so it stands still.
  M1.wheel.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The wheel has its own water supply. That's why the mill can grind with the sluice shut — as long as the pond is full.
  M1.bench.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    [slowly] Pavel's tools: hammers, a chisel, a plane. Everything in its place — all covered in shavings, or perhaps flour.
  H2d.stand_zm.mount narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The office mirror fits into Dunya's stand. The wedges still need tapping in to secure the loose frame.
  H2d.office_mirror.clamped narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The wedges are seated. The glass clears — it shows the office as it is now: the inside of the door, bolt in its brackets.
  H2d.office_mirror.view_first narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The mill office is visible in the glass. Not a sound.
  H2d.office_mirror.view_again narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The mill office in the glass. The same silence.
  H2d.office_mirror.glass_touch narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    My hand meets glass. No way through.
  H2d.office_mirror.glass_loose narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The frame has loosened. The glass trembles and clouds over. The wedges need tapping in.
  H2d.office_mirror.bell_mute narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The bell is mute without its clapper. In Dunya's hand, the label says: "Clapper in the attic chest."
  H2d.office_mirror.bell_unclamped narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Secure the frame first. Without the wedges driven in, I can't see anything through the glass.
  H2d.office_mirror.hook_slipped narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The hook slipped. Pavel lifts it and starts again.
  H2d.bell.hang narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The clapper fits. The bell is as good as new again.
  H2d.bell.need_mirror narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    I must ring and watch the office mirror. But it isn't on the stand yet.
  H2d.nina_mirror.clamp narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    [warmly] The clamp draws the frame together. Slowly, the cloudy glass begins to clear…
  H2d.nina_mirror.knock_first narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    [sad] Agata knocks on the glass — no answer. Mama can't hear her.
  H2d.nina_mirror.watch_wait narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The clock hand has barely moved. I need to watch longer.
  E4.M23d.prompt narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Who should tell Tikhon about Dunya?
  E5.windlass.laid narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The beam settles onto the old plate's ring. Just where the bridge beam rested before the flood.
  E5.M25.prompt narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    What shall I carve on the end?
  EP.place_bridge narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    The bridge
  H1d.nina_coat.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Her coat on Dunya's own hook. Mama brought it home from Olkhovka.
  H1d.nina_coat.look_done narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Dunya's coat hangs on its own hook. The sleeve is mended now.
  H1d.nina_coat.prompt narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    How shall I mend it?
  H1d.tea_corner.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Dunya's kettle is on the windowsill. Mama is here; we could have some tea.
  H1d.tea_corner.go_home narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Dunya's kettle went on the stove. We called the family to tea — Tamara and Ulyana came, too.
  H1d.tea_corner.go_all narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    We took Dunya's kettle to Mama's parlour. Everyone who came outside was invited to tea.
  H1d.tea_corner.prompt narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Where shall we have our first tea together?
  H2q.second_bench.look narrator  ru           ZAKADR     eleven_v4    Ilya and Mitya brought the second bench from Ilya's workshop. There are two in Dunya's now.
